{
  "_comment": "The core of the shex.js 'examples manifest' vocabulary -- packages/*/examples/manifest.yaml, aggregated by tools/aggregate-manifests.js into doc/tests-manifest.yaml and read by tools/manifest-runner.js. This is NOT the shexTest conformance-manifest vocabulary (node_modules/shex-test/context.jsonld, mf:/sht:/sx:): that is a real, RDF-based format shared with other ShEx implementations (PyShEx, the Scala and Rust implementations). This one is shex.js's own ad hoc webapp/example-gallery convention, which grew one key at a time and has no shared vocabulary backing it -- this file is a first sketch at giving it one, reusing shexTest's terms where the meaning is genuinely the same (schema, data, shape, node/focus, comment) so the two can be crosswalked, and minting shex.js's own terms both for the conventions shexTest has no concept of (URL variants, labels, the query-map DSL, plugin loading, neighborhood selection) AND for the one place a shex.js term looks like a shexTest one but is not: `status` here is the expected validation VERDICT (conformant/nonconformant), while shexTest's mf:status is the TEST'S OWN curation status (mf:Approved/mf:Proposed/...) -- shexTest encodes the verdict structurally instead, via rdf:type (sht:ValidationTest vs sht:ValidationFailure). Aliasing shex.js's status to mf:status would have been a false cognate, not a crosswalk, so it gets its own shexjs:status term instead; a real crosswalk would need to turn an entry's status into its @type, which is future work past this sketch. A manifest entry stacks this context with the neighborhood- and extension-specific ones it needs (see packages/neighborhood-*/manifest-context.jsonld in this repository, and https://shexspec.github.io/extensions/*/manifest-context.jsonld beside each extension's spec in shexSpec/extensions -- which tools/yamlld-to-nested-turtle.js reads from a sibling checkout until that site publishes them), each contributing one namespace prefix. Those attributes are LEXICALLY SCOPED: an entry writes a neighborhood's or extension's attributes under one `<prefix>:parms` key whose value is a mapping (map:parms, sparql:parms, wikibase:parms), and that prefix's context defines the mapping's keys through a JSON-LD 1.1 property-scoped @context, so inside it they are written bare (outputSchemaURL, endpoint) and still expand to the namespace's IRIs, while outside it the same bare key is undefined and dropped -- the prefix is written once per entry, not once per attribute, and an attribute can't be confused with a same-named one from another extension because it is only defined inside its own scope. In RDF the entry gets one <prefix>:parms arc to a blank node holding them (doc/tests-manifest-ld.ttl shows the graph). NOTE: this top-level _comment sits beside @context, not inside it -- a JSON-LD context's own term values may only be strings or objects, never arrays, so this is deliberately here instead.",

  "@context": {
    "mf": "http://www.w3.org/2001/sw/DataAccess/tests/test-manifest#",
    "sx": "https://shexspec.github.io/shexTest/ns#",
    "rdfs": "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#",
    "shexjs": "https://shex.io/ns/examples-manifest#",

    "entries": {"@id": "mf:entries", "@container": "@list"},

    "schemaLabel": "shexjs:schemaLabel",
    "dataLabel": "shexjs:dataLabel",
    "comment": "rdfs:comment",

    "status": "shexjs:status",

    "schema": {"@id": "sx:schema"},
    "schemaURL": {"@id": "sx:schema", "@type": "@id"},
    "data": {"@id": "sx:data"},
    "dataURL": {"@id": "sx:data", "@type": "@id", "@container": "@set"},

    "node": {"@id": "sx:focus", "@type": "@id"},
    "shape": {"@id": "sx:shape", "@type": "@id"},
    "queryMap": "shexjs:queryMap",
    "queryMapURL": {"@id": "shexjs:queryMap", "@type": "@id"},

    "overlay": "shexjs:overlay",
    "overlayURL": {"@id": "shexjs:overlay", "@type": "@id"},

    "plugins": {"@id": "shexjs:plugins", "@type": "@id", "@container": "@list"},

    "neighborhood": "shexjs:neighborhood",
    "dataBase": {"@id": "shexjs:dataBase", "@type": "@id"},

    "slurp": "shexjs:slurp"
  }
}
